 "justification": "The bias-free field anomaly repeats on the same section (mean r 0.688, 5/7 pairs beat phase surrogates at p < 0.05; different-section null mean 0.388). Driving proxies explain a median 47% of it (the train's own traction field), but the residual still repeats (mean r 0.533, 6/7 significant, null mean 0.224, p95 0.427), also in the mid-section away from the pull-away traction peak (mean r 0.587, 4/7 significant, null p95 0.584). So there is a position-locked component, modest and not yet separable from non-linear traction effects that repeat because drivers run each section alike. Use it as a low-weight DTW feature; the ablation decides. |B| itself stays NO-GO.",
